  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025-2026 Chronic Crisis: Building Resilience Capacity of Pastoralist in Somali Region, Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project in Somali Region focuses on water management, livelihoods, food security, and capacity building by rehabilitating infrastructure and transitioning to sustainable solutions like solar-powered water systems. It promotes WASH improvements, health education, climate-sensitive disease prevention, and nutrition programs. Cross-cutting themes include protection, gender inclusion, community engagement, and climate resilience. The initiative integrates digitalization for efficiency and strengthens ERCS&#x2019;s capacity through training and emergency preparedness. Mental health and psychosocial support services are also prioritized, ensuring safe referrals and PSS activities. The overall goal is sustainable, community-led development, enhancing resilience against climate change and crises.</narrative>
  </description>
